    "DisplayName": "Stratus",
    "Notes": "A featureless sheet a few hundred metres thick, sitting almost on the ground. EdgeTopFraction 0.88 because a sheet does not thin into a pad at its rim, and the erosion is halved because what makes stratus stratus is that it has no edge to speak of. Placement scale 4.00: a sheet has no cells. Pushing the period to four times the layer's tile is how a type says 'I am one patch as far as you can see' without a second kind of coverage field.",
